$search / $serch — web search via DuckDuckGo (results as JSON in texts[])

Also available as $search (preferred).

SUMMARY
  Runs each input prompt as a search query through DuckDuckGo and appends one
  texts[] link per query containing a JSON array of {url, text} objects.

SYNTAX
  $serch
  $serch(limit=10)
  $serch(limit=25, lang='en', region='us')

INPUT
  prompts[] — search query strings (instruction body counts if no prompt links).

OUTPUT
  texts[] — one .json-style .txt per query:
    [
      {"url": "https://…", "text": "title and snippet"},
      …
    ]

ARGUMENTS
  limit=    — max results 1–100 (default 10)
  lang=     — language hint for region code (e.g. en, de)
  region=   — region / market (e.g. us, uk) or full kl code (e.g. us-en)
  site=     — restrict to site (e.g. github.com)
  timeout=  — HTTP timeout seconds (default 60)

BACKEND
  Primary: DuckDuckGo HTML search (https://html.duckduckgo.com/html/)
  Fallback: DuckDuckGo Instant Answer API (https://api.duckduckgo.com/)

ENVIRONMENT
  AH_EMULATE_SERCH=1 — fake results, no HTTP.
  AH_SERCH_KL=us-en  — override DuckDuckGo locale (kl) parameter.

EXAMPLE
  @news: $serch(limit=5)
  latest AI agent frameworks 2026

PROMPT-CONSUMING
  Yes.
